     "result_text_tail": "break the runway rule.\n- **\"Contribution per order\"** means after the site's fixed cost. Where the pop-up didn't report a cost line (goods margin, fee, picking, payment), I used the benchmark value.\n\n**Sourcing:**\n- **Sources:** all 169 numbers come from the briefing pack or are calculated from it, with live formulas in the workbook. A script confirmed all 65 quoted passages appear word for word in the pack.\n- **Grades:** shown numbers are grade B (119) or E (9, our own estimates). None reach A, because a second source isn't possible without web research.\n- **Findings:** of the 11 hypotheses tested, 1 held up (market growth), 1 was partly right (rider pay: the plan only holds up to $24.81 an hour), and 9 were wrong.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Visual check:** LibreOffice isn't installed here, so I couldn't view the slides as images. I relied on the renderer's layout checks, which now report nothing, and on reading the rendered text.\n- **Display rounding:** most dollar figures on slides show one decimal, so the median loss reads \"$6.2\" rather than $6.17. One equation slide carries a note that its cards are rounded.\n\nThe QA check passes with two warnings left on purpose. They flag the two market hypotheses as things the board can't influence, but I kept them because they answer the founders' own claims.\n\nNext, I could switch the theme, or cut a shorter 10-slide version for the board pre-read.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- `parcelbird-now.pptx`\n- `parcelbird-now-sources.xlsx`"
    }
